    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate dynamics",
    "problem": "Natural variability from atmospheric circulation complicates the interpretation of observed temperature trends, obscuring the underlying externally forced climate signal and creating discrepancies between observations and climate model simulations.",
    "method": "A trajectory-based regression method is applied to ERA5 reanalysis data to quantify the effect of atmospheric circulation on temperature trends by statistically relating daily temperature anomalies to the three-dimensional origin of air masses arriving at a location.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the effect of atmospheric circulation on monthly, seasonal, and annual surface air temperature trends from 1979\u20132018 by applying a trajectory-based method to ERA5 reanalysis data.",
    "model": [
        "CMIP5"
    ],
